WEBVTT

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:07.520
Wow, so many people in line.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:12.860
I don't know much about exhibition sale fairs, and yet I'm here...

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:14.430
But we get to sell here.

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:15.370
That's right.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:19.520
We went through hell
to finish our game last night...

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:21.530
for everyone who's here today!

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:24.190
President!

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:25.120
Shii!

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:26.780
Are you okay, President?!

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:30.740
You're burning up!

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:34.090
I can't go on. So I'm passing on...

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:38.350
the treasured items entrusted to me
by my predecessor.

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:39.710
President!

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:45.770
President!

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:52.650
Please take care, President.

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:54.930
<i>I know.</i>

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:59.620
<i>She has the power to come down with
a cold before something she wants to avoid.</i>

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.950
Make sure you're in
this year's sports festival!

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:03.710
Even I...

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:06.080
What? You caught a cold again?!

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:09.240
Will the president be okay?

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:12.160
She's strong enough to make it home to rest.

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:14.450
Well, let's go back to the hall.

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:16.720
We have to set up our booth quickly!

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:17.900
O-okay!

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:06.140
Can you take out the set-up supplies
from that package you got?

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:07.180
Okay!

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:09.560
Oh, so that's what she meant
by "treasured items."

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:15.680
These are treasured items, pyon.

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:19.450
That belonged to the previous president.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:33.920
Hello...

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:35.820
Good luck to you.

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:38.480
Oh, thanks! You too.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:43.010
The "Doujin Disc-Only"
exhibition sale is officially open.

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:48.340
I-it's begun!

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:51.980
Please, no pushing or running.

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:57.030
Having people see my drawings
is nerve-wracking, after all.

00:03:57.030 --> 00:04:00.240
You just have to collect 300 yen
if they want to buy a disc.

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:03.880
If they pay with a 1,000-yen bill,
I give them 700 in change.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:04.960
Right!

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:16.090
They won't come right away.

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:17.230
You don't need change yet.

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:23.300
Everyone here has created a game
or has come to buy one, right?

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:24.560
Yeah.

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:26.580
So many people...

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:26.960
Oh!

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:28.520
Yumine!

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:32.320
Tama-chan! So this is the event
you mentioned?

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:35.080
Sorry, I can't stop by right now.

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:40.910
There's a huge line for Temawari-sensei's new work, so I have to hurry there.

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:43.370
See you later!

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:51.520
Everyone's drawings are awesome!

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:55.130
Bold artwork really draws your attention.

00:04:55.130 --> 00:04:57.550
If people aren't interested
in our disc...

00:04:57.550 --> 00:05:00.340
is it because my drawings are...?

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:02.060
No, it's not that.

00:05:02.470 --> 00:05:08.140
People create posters, showy exhibits, and let people try out their game...

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:09.770
There are ways to attract attention.

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:11.850
But what's really important...

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:14.480
is that we didn't do any marketing...

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.740
We didn't even mention it
on the internet!

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:21.570
Well, that's how exhibition sales are.

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:24.640
This is the first time
we've entered this event.

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:28.720
And you did your very best,
didn't you, Honda-san?

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:32.710
Yes, but...

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:38.800
Here... look at your dad's picture
and cheer up.

00:05:39.090 --> 00:05:41.240
I'm gonna go around
and draw up some sales.

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:45.720
I'm sure there are people I know.
So wait here and draw.

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:57.280
<i>Seki-senpai was trying to be nice to me.</i>

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:01.650
Hey, long time no see.

00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:03.320
We produced a visual novel.

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:06.160
Awesome! Let's exchange discs.

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:09.780
<i>Everyone's had my back since yesterday.</i>

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:12.600
<i>I have to thank them.</i>

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:20.080
Oh, I'm sorry!

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:29.310
<i>Is it okay for me to stay here and just draw?</i>

00:06:29.640 --> 00:06:31.970
<i>Is it okay to just sit here?</i>

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:35.450
Excuse me.

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:38.210
Hello?

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:40.170
Excuse me...

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:41.420
Oh, yes?

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:42.710
<i>Someone stopped!</i>

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:45.880
Are you the one
who did the artwork for this?

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:47.130
Yes...

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:48.670
I'm...

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:50.930
sorry.

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:56.060
Everyone else's creations are
really wonderful.

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:59.600
<i>Mine is nothing like theirs...</i>

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:02.610
I'll take one.

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:06.820
I really love drawings like this.

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:10.200
And, if you don't mind...

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:13.680
I'm back! I traded lots of discs—

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:15.370
Oh, Seki-senpai!

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:19.370
W-what does
"can I get a sketch" mean?

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:21.620
She wants you to do
a sketch right now.

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:24.500
Me? Draw in her sketchbook?

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:25.090
Yes.

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:28.800
Oh, only if you don't mind.

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:31.550
A-are you sure
you want me to draw?

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:34.220
Please... take ten of these...

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:35.380
Hey!

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:43.150
Um, it doesn't have to be right now.
I can come back later.

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:44.690
O-okay, sure!

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:49.610
Thank you!

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:54.450
Honda-san, we sold another one!

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:57.540
People tend to browse around more
in the afternoon, after all.

00:07:59.820 --> 00:08:03.750
That lady just now in the business suit
must work for a corporation.

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:06.360
I guess even people like her
come to exhibition sales.

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:12.050
I know you're happy,
but some kind of response would be nice.

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:14.470
Hello, I'll take one.

00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:16.010
Ah, Yumine!

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:18.260
Wait. But first...

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:19.810
What?

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:21.810
I love the bunny ears,
so I want some pics.

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:25.270
Don't move!

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:32.150
Don't hide your face!

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:33.740
No!

00:08:34.260 --> 00:08:35.660
Come on!

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:37.410
Done!

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:40.830
But will she be happy with this?

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:43.120
Oh, how pretty!

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:48.630
You did such a detailed drawing.
Thank you.

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:51.210
Um, is this really okay?

00:08:51.210 --> 00:08:53.590
Of course! I'll treasure it.

00:08:55.470 --> 00:08:58.050
In fact, can you autograph it?

00:08:58.050 --> 00:09:02.560
A-autographs? I've never even thought
about that...

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:06.520
Okay then... How about a comment
about what you're feeling?

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:07.650
Then...!

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:12.740
Papa... I'm so happy right now!

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:13.780
"Papa?!"

00:09:15.030 --> 00:09:16.760
Thank you very much!

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:18.760
No, thank you!

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:21.220
Honda-san, turn this way.

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:22.040
Yes?

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:25.250
What's that for?!

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:27.920
Sorry, you looked so cute,
I couldn't help it.

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:30.130
Please email it to me too.

00:09:47.390 --> 00:09:52.190
<i>The "Doujin Disc-Only"
exhibition sale is now closed.</i>

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:55.900
We sold thirteen copies today!
That's great.

00:09:56.570 --> 00:09:59.570
Actually, we traded nine.
So we sold four copies.

00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:01.780
Although one was to Fuda-san.

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:05.330
Oh, it's an email from Fujikawa-senpai.

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:07.210
She's heading over here now.

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:11.130
Oh yeah? Then she can help us
break down.

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:16.760
Oh and... we'd better let
Teru-senpai know how it went today.

00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:22.220
Oh, they seem to be having fun.

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:26.730
This business suit costume
really hugs my hips.

00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:28.520
But I'm glad I came today.

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:34.110
Everyone, including Kitten,
are doing their best.

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:37.530
I think I'll be able to
lend them a hand again.

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:47.910
Honda-chan, good job!

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:49.080
Fujikawa-senpai!

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:51.880
Hi. How did sales go?

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:54.210
Yes! We sold a few.

00:10:54.210 --> 00:10:56.300
That's how it is the first time.

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:57.970
And get this!

00:10:57.970 --> 00:11:00.800
Today, someone actually asked me for a sketch!

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:04.260
Wow. That's terrific, Honda-chan!
Did it turn out nicely?

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:08.230
Yes, although the face could
have been a bit more balanced.

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:11.310
And where's the scenario writer?

00:11:11.310 --> 00:11:12.900
Seki-senpai is...

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:14.860
Rock...

00:11:15.090 --> 00:11:16.730
Paper...

00:11:18.150 --> 00:11:21.230
One more time!

00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:26.790
They're doing rock-paper-scissors
for the post-event prizes.

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:30.120
I've never seen anyone
so serious about rock-paper-scissors.

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:41.130
If I stuck paper four times
in a row...

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:44.390
I would've won the limited goods
I missed out on last year.

00:11:44.390 --> 00:11:46.470
You're still upset about that?

00:11:46.470 --> 00:11:50.390
You know, your fixation on
anime goods is a bit unexpected.

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:52.480
I haven't been open
about it lately,

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:55.940
but I admit I'm a real otaku.

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:59.940
To be honest, even this hair ornament
is from an anime.

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:02.070
Oh, really?

00:12:02.070 --> 00:12:05.160
You're right, the anime title
is on the back.

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:08.240
But what a great event.
It was so lively.

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:11.080
It made me want to
publish my own novel.

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:15.170
There were so many great artists,
I was in awe.

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:17.590
You should've come, Fujikawa-san.

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:21.970
After I sent the music
to Murakami-san last night,

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:24.760
I slept for 17 hours straight
and just got up.

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:25.930
That's too much sleep.

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:27.760
Oh, it's from Shii.

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:28.720
President?

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:29.640
Hello?

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:32.850
Aya... how did the exhibition sale go...?

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:35.900
Shii, are you okay?

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:37.650
I think so.

00:12:39.110 --> 00:12:42.280
My temperature is 37.2°C.

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:45.280
I was just overwhelmed
by the crowd, that's all.

00:12:45.610 --> 00:12:48.330
But if this does prove fatal...

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:52.370
or I can't leave the house,
I don't want to be a burden on you...

00:12:52.710 --> 00:12:55.290
So I wanted to apologize first.

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:59.090
Okay, okay. Just get some rest.

00:12:59.090 --> 00:13:00.500
Take care.

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:03.010
Murakami-san wasn't here because...

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:07.550
At the station this morning, she said that such a crowd was tough on her and went back.

00:13:07.550 --> 00:13:09.470
37.2 is normal.

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:12.120
Never mind already.
Let's talk about a wrap party!

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:14.520
But what about the president?

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:16.600
She'll be fine
in a couple of days.

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:20.940
Sounds great. How about we come
to your house this weekend, Seki-san?

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:22.940
My house?

00:13:22.940 --> 00:13:25.450
Please, Iris-sensei.

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:27.160
Don't call me by my username.

00:13:28.280 --> 00:13:30.700
And how long are you going to
wear the bunny ears?

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:34.750
My muscles are so sore.

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:35.870
Where?

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:39.040
<i>With everyone's help,
I made a lot of drawings.</i>

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:42.210
<i>And somehow,
we finished creating a game.</i>

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:47.130
<i>I'm still new to drawing
and have lots to learn,</i>

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:51.760
<i>but just maybe, lots of people
will know about us one day.</i>

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:56.270
<i>A thought like that
gives me a bit of a thrill.</i>

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:05.860
<i>The weekend came and
we wrapped up at Seki-senpai's house.</i>

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:08.700
<i>Yumine was a special guest.</i>

00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:10.870
Who is...

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:12.700
the king?!

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:16.000
That's me? What do I do?

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:18.330
Wow! You're the perfect one, President!

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:20.420
Make a speech like a king.

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:23.000
Well, let me offer my greeting.

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:26.590
Thank you for coming today
to mark the completion of the SNS...

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:27.620
You're too formal!

00:14:27.910 --> 00:14:32.220
But when I became president,
I was so worried.

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:36.560
And thanks to Honda-san and all of you,
we completed our game.

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:39.310
Yeah well, this is
an emotional moment.

00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:43.940
I hope, little by little, all kinds of
people can play our games...

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:46.530
That's the kind of club
I want us to be.

00:14:46.900 --> 00:14:49.200
I'll keep doing my best.

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:50.910
So will I, from the sidelines.

00:14:50.910 --> 00:14:52.480
By the way, where's Fujikawa-san?

00:14:52.760 --> 00:14:56.700
Fujikawa-senpai said she just came up
with a neat melody.

00:14:56.700 --> 00:14:58.580
E... G#... A... G#...

00:14:58.580 --> 00:14:59.670
Way to ruin the moment!

00:14:59.670 --> 00:15:02.000
Who's the king?!

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:04.290
I am the king.

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:06.380
Okay, then...

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:09.340
Why don't we play the game
you created?

00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:11.890
I'd like tips on tackling
the hard part.

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:13.800
Hey, great idea!

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:17.700
If I see my artwork now,
I'd only find flaws...

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:22.480
It'd be kind of embarrassing
to hear my own lines being read...

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:25.570
There was a bug in the code
during that desperate rush...

00:15:25.570 --> 00:15:27.730
I guess the nays have it.

00:15:27.730 --> 00:15:28.860
Oh dear...

00:15:29.190 --> 00:15:31.280
I'm the next king.

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:34.990
Oh yeah, I have something
to say to Honda-chan.

00:15:34.990 --> 00:15:35.870
Me?

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:40.460
I'm sorry we made a newbie like you
stay up all night and work so hard.

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:43.880
And, I hear you defended me.

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:45.210
Oh, no...

00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:48.460
We were all feeling cornered that time.

00:15:48.460 --> 00:15:52.630
But doing my best with everyone
was really fun.

00:15:52.630 --> 00:15:56.080
You're such a good girl, Tama-chan.

00:15:56.080 --> 00:15:58.850
Hey, don't abuse your position, King!

00:15:58.850 --> 00:16:00.300
Aw, come on!

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:02.730
It's just a little skinship.

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:04.940
Tama-chan is... not like that!

00:16:05.650 --> 00:16:08.570
You don't know anything
about Tama-chan!

00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:11.900
But I know, since I've watched her
since grade school!

00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:14.660
Tama-chan's the seme!

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:20.950
If she were a boy character,
she'd always be the seme!

00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:23.580
Oh, and Fujikawa-senpai,
you'd be the sasoi-uke.

00:16:23.580 --> 00:16:25.210
Is it necessary to change into boys?

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:28.000
Seki-senpai, you agree, don't you?

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:30.170
W-why ask me?!

00:16:30.670 --> 00:16:33.800
It's just a hunch, but you fantasize
like this too, right?

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:35.970
I'm saying that you can't reverse the order of a pairing.

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:37.890
Y-you think so?

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:40.640
Um... What do they mean by "seme?"

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:42.140
I wonder...

00:16:42.140 --> 00:16:45.270
Calling a good girl like you a "seme?"

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:46.960
No, listen...

00:16:46.960 --> 00:16:51.240
Even a character who looks like an angel
has pent-up passion inside...

00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:54.660
She'd awaken in derivative works, and it's that gap moe...

00:16:57.320 --> 00:16:59.200
Wait, what're you trying to make me say?!

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:02.700
Okay, I'm the king!

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:04.710
Forget this last subject!

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:08.210
Hey, Seki-senpai, let's talk raunchy.

00:17:08.210 --> 00:17:09.940
Won't talk! Won't write!
It's forgotten.

00:17:10.210 --> 00:17:12.260
Seriously? You want to forget?

00:17:12.260 --> 00:17:14.220
What is it, Shii?

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:16.760
When you were in the Literature Club...

00:17:17.090 --> 00:17:21.800
Teru-senpai read your story and liked it,
so she suggested making a game.

00:17:22.080 --> 00:17:24.560
That was what
this club was built on.

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:26.580
Can you really take it so lightly?

00:17:26.580 --> 00:17:27.850
Err, well...

00:17:28.610 --> 00:17:29.770
And so...

00:17:29.770 --> 00:17:32.280
Let's read aloud stories from the past.

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:34.240
The anthology
from middle school.

00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:36.360
Stop it!

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:39.660
I want to hear stories
from your past.

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:40.660
Sure thing.

00:17:42.950 --> 00:17:47.040
Fujikawa-san always looked angry
in the beginning.

00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:50.280
Until the ninth grade, she talked like a boy.

00:17:51.250 --> 00:17:54.210
And you were always
so nervous, Murakami-san.

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:56.550
That's right! In Home Econ
in fifth grade...

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:59.260
We're not talking that far back
in our past!

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:02.430
Seems like an insurrection, King.

00:18:02.430 --> 00:18:05.980
We should change the subject...
to something more cheerful!

00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:07.940
Oh, I know!

00:18:08.560 --> 00:18:11.440
Let's talk love stories! I'll start.

00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:13.400
I love my papa.

00:18:13.670 --> 00:18:17.030
He praised the game we created.

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:21.580
Huh?

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:24.370
Tama-chan, you just want to talk fondly
about your dad.

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:27.370
I don't like talking about myself...
It's sorta tactless.

00:18:27.370 --> 00:18:29.580
It's too soon for me.

00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:33.880
Fujikawa-san, I'll bet you have a story.
From your DTM bunch.

00:18:34.670 --> 00:18:36.540
Strange as it may seem, I don't.

00:18:36.880 --> 00:18:40.390
Though I think I'm pretty good-looking.

00:18:40.390 --> 00:18:43.120
Maybe, I'm too cute and
no one wants to approach me.

00:18:43.120 --> 00:18:44.000
Just kidding.

00:18:45.020 --> 00:18:46.640
The drop at around 300 hertz...

00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:50.770
Oh yeah, she's unapproachable.
Composing with that scary expression.

00:18:52.110 --> 00:18:55.360
I received a love letter once...

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:57.340
Seriously? I've never heard about it.

00:18:57.780 --> 00:18:59.890
It was around second grade.

00:18:59.890 --> 00:19:02.490
I gave it a lot of thought...

00:19:02.490 --> 00:19:06.080
And I couldn't believe anyone
would love me...

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:09.210
I thought maybe it was
some mistake.

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:10.920
Or maybe it was a dare or penalty.

00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:14.380
I was sweet-talked into showing up
and taken off guard.

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:17.420
I have no idea why, but...

00:19:17.420 --> 00:19:20.430
maybe my presence alone
was unpleasant to him.

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:23.260
So I handed it to my teacher.

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:25.760
What should I do, Sensei?

00:19:25.760 --> 00:19:28.430
Are you okay?
Did something bad happen to you?!

00:19:28.430 --> 00:19:31.810
You're so negative! And the way
you dealt with it was harsh!

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:35.610
<i>After this and that, the party came to an end.</i>

00:19:36.070 --> 00:19:41.410
I wonder if they'll tell me about
Teru-senpai, who formed this club?

00:19:41.410 --> 00:19:42.700
I think that's up to you, Tama-chan.

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:48.200
Oh, that's right. Seki-senpai said those
items belonged to Teru-senpai.

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:57.050
Huh? What is it?

00:19:57.550 --> 00:19:59.670
I'm the king.

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:03.430
Hey, that thing never
looks good on you.

00:20:03.430 --> 00:20:04.550
I'm aware of that.

00:20:04.760 --> 00:20:06.450
You're taking it off?

00:20:06.450 --> 00:20:09.960
The former president gave it to you, right?

00:20:09.960 --> 00:20:12.920
The fact that you kept it all this time even though it doesn't suit you...

00:20:12.920 --> 00:20:16.570
means that you treasure it too, right?

00:20:22.570 --> 00:20:23.570
It's our secret.

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:27.280
It looks best on you, Honda-chan.
The bunny ears.

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:38.110
So Tama-chan, you showed your dad
the game you created?

00:20:38.110 --> 00:20:41.300
Yup. It's something I accomplished
with the club, after all.

00:20:41.880 --> 00:20:43.800
Stella no Mahou...

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:45.300
Huh? Did you say something?

00:20:45.300 --> 00:20:47.180
No, it's nothing.

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:49.870
Huh... How nice...

00:20:49.870 --> 00:20:53.640
My family isn't that open-minded
about subcultures like this.

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:57.610
One time, I was told to get rid of my manga
and we had a huge fight.

00:20:58.150 --> 00:21:01.990
I stood my ground, telling them that
it didn't affect my grades.

00:21:02.280 --> 00:21:06.570
In the end, my parents gave in
and now, they tolerate it.

00:21:06.570 --> 00:21:12.160
Then if that happens to me, I'll convince
Papa with lots of drawings of old men.

00:21:12.160 --> 00:21:14.540
Tama-chan...
Seriously that's what you'd do?

00:21:14.810 --> 00:21:18.960
Oh sorry, Yumine.
I have to stop at the stationery shop.

00:21:18.960 --> 00:21:20.750
I'll tag along.

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:24.960
But it might take time,
and you have a curfew, right?

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:27.760
Okay then, let's part here.

00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:29.140
See you!

00:21:29.140 --> 00:21:30.720
Yes, see you.

00:21:31.680 --> 00:21:34.180
<i>A club that creates doujin games.</i>

00:21:34.460 --> 00:21:39.110
<i>It seems hectic, with lots of work
and last-minute spurts...</i>

00:21:39.940 --> 00:21:45.110
<i>But Tama-chan has a glowing smile,
and I think that's wonderful.</i>

00:21:46.030 --> 00:21:47.530
I'll take this.

00:23:22.960 --> 00:23:26.170
That I will love you forever.

00:23:26.170 --> 00:23:26.800
I love you!

00:23:26.800 --> 00:23:28.090
I have to sort it out!

00:23:28.090 --> 00:23:28.720
Really?

00:23:28.720 --> 00:23:29.550
A child?

00:23:29.550 --> 00:23:32.160
How dare you make a fool of me that time!
